📖 Usage Guide
1. Standard Scan (Direct / No Proxy)
Fastest mode. Your IP is visible to the target.

python scanner.py

2. Anonymous Scan (Via Tor)
Hides your IP. Requires Tor to be running (see Prerequisite).

python scanner.py --tor

Scans default ports (1-1000). To scan all ports:

python scanner.py --tor -p 1-65535

3. Anonymous Scan (Custom SOCKS5 Proxy)
Use this if you don't have Tor but have a SOCKS5 proxy (e.g., from a VPN or private server).

python scanner.py --proxy socks5h://127.0.0.1:9050

(Replace 127.0.0.1:9050 with your proxy IP and Port)

⚙️ Advanced Options
How to Change the Target IP
Use the -t flag to scan a specific IP or Hostname.

Scan your router: python scanner.py --tor -t 192.168.1.1
Scan a specific server: python scanner.py --tor -t 10.0.0.5
How to Change Port Range
Use the -p flag to define the range. Format: START-END.

Scan common ports only: python scanner.py --tor -p 1-1024
Scan a specific range: python scanner.py --tor -p 20-100
Scan ALL ports: python scanner.py --tor -p 1-65535 (Note: This takes longer via Tor)
Full Command Example
Scan all ports on 192.168.1.50 using Tor:

python scanner.py --tor -t 192.168.1.50 -p 1-65535

